# Rust build artifacts. 2.4GB and fully regenerable with `cargo build`.
/target/

# Node dependencies. 150MB, regenerable with `npm install`.
node_modules/

# Vendored reference repos.
#
# These were read to answer specific architecture questions and the answers are
# written up in spikes/*/FINDINGS.md and STATUS.md. They are ~376MB of upstream
# source, of which joplin-dev alone is 272MB, and nothing in the build imports
# them. They are deliberately NOT tracked: if you need to consult one again,
# re-fetch that single repo rather than carrying all six in the tree.
#
#   joplin-dev, cryptpad-main   — read for sync/storage patterns only
#   tiptap-main                  — read for the pagination/virtualisation audit
#   loro-main                    — read for the CRDT API and perf tests
#   taino-edit-main              — read for the Rust-editor capability audit
#   crdt-richtext-main           — read for the Peritext/Fugue prototype audit
Github_projects_worth_forking/

# Vite / build output
dist/
.vite/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local databases and WAL sidecars. A user's documents must never be committed.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# Tauri shell build output
crates/holonomy-shell/gen/schemas/
# The engine verification writes here; it is a per-run artifact, not source.
target/verification-report.json
